<figure id="S3.F3" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:50%;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01879v1/wiki.svg" id="S3.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/110;" width="229" height="110"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="S3.F3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Average Editing Performance of WikiBigEdit Across Different Models</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 3.2 Main Results ‣ 3 Experiments" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> effevtively addressed <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Q1</span>, <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Q4</span> and <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Q5</span>. It has been rigorously evaluated across diverse models and scales (N = 1, 30, 120, 1000) of QA editing tasks, demonstrating state-of-the-art performance. Fine-tuning-based methods achieve good accuracy and generalization at small scales but suffer from catastrophic forgetting and knowledge conflicts in large-scale edits, leading to performance degradation. GRACE excels in accuracy but has limited generalization, while WISE maintains strong locality but sacrifices critical knowledge, reducing editing accuracy. ROME-style methods are stable but overfit and struggle with generalization.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To address <span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Q2</span>, Table <a href="#S3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 3.2 Main Results ‣ 3 Experiments" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> shows REPAIR’s effectiveness in reducing hallucinations on the SelfCheckGPT dataset for LLaMA-3-8B across different editing scales. REPAIR balances reduced hallucinations with preserved locality, making it highly effective for large-scale model editing.</p>
</div>
