<td id="A3.T8.5.12.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:2.0pt;padding-right:2.0pt;"><math id="A3.T8.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.68\pm 0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.800em">0.68</mn><mo mathsize="0.800em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.68\pm 0.02</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.01879v1/relative_cost_vs_best_loglog.png" id="A3.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/254;" width="381" height="254" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A3.F7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Cost-Performance Assessment.<span id="A3.F7.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The total runtime of each method scales approximately linearly with the editing scale <math id="A3.F7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, appearing as straight lines with slopes close to 1 in log-log coordinates. This indicates that the primary overhead is proportional to the number of edited entries.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Under identical hardware and batch configurations, the WISE baseline exhibits lower per-unit overhead. REPAIR demonstrates a similar scaling slope but with a higher intercept, primarily attributable to:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Distribution-aware clustering and reorganization;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Additional forward/backward passes for in-batch distillation;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The triggering frequency and cost of closed-loop pruning and retraining at large scales;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The final <span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">merging (TIES)</span> cost.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> increases, the runtime curves of ROME, MEND, and FT-L exhibit significantly steeper growth, becoming substantially expensive or nearly infeasible at <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Throughput</span> demonstrates that WISE maintains approximately <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 1.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>1.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 1.8</annotation></semantics></math> edits/min at large <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, followed by GRACE. REPAIR achieves <math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 0.8</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="A3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9</annotation></semantics></math> edits/min at scale, lower than WISE and MEMIT-M, consistent with expectations given its additional computational procedures.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Error bars (representing standard deviation across multiple runs) indicate that REPAIR exhibits slightly higher variance than WISE, attributable to fluctuations in retriggering frequency and sample distribution characteristics.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Relative overhead</span> shows the time ratio of REPAIR to WISE increasing from <math id="A3.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sim 1.6\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∼</mo><mn>1.6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 1.6\times</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.p6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sim 2.2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∼</mo><mn>2.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 2.2\times</annotation></semantics></math> with increasing scale.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Theoretical Analysis and Proof Sketches</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now provide theoretical justifications for the stability and convergence of the proposed REPAIR framework. We introduce formal assumptions and derive lemmas and theorems that characterize the behavior of our method.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#43C67A;">D.1  Preliminaries</h3>

<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Standard Optimization Setting)<span id="Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We assume that the loss function <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\Theta_{1})-\nabla\mathcal{L}(\Theta_{2})\|\leq L\|\Theta_{1}-\Theta_{2}\|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\Theta_{1})-\nabla\mathcal{L}(\Theta_{2})\|\leq L\|\Theta_{1}-\Theta_{2}\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and bounded below by <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{*}&gt;-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{*}&gt;-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Learning rates satisfy <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\eta_{t}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\eta_{t}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\eta_{t}^{2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\eta_{t}^{2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#43C67A;">D.2  Stability of Masked Gradient Updates</h3>

<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Norm Bound under Masked Updates)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}=\nabla_{W_{v,i}^{\prime}}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}=\nabla_{W_{v,i}^{\prime}}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Bernoulli mask. Then the masked update</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{v,i}^{\prime}=-\eta(M_{i}\odot g_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{v,i}^{\prime}=-\eta(M_{i}\odot g_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfies <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta W_{v,i}^{\prime}\|_{2}\leq\eta\|g_{i}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta W_{v,i}^{\prime}\|_{2}\leq\eta\|g_{i}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a coordinate projection, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}\odot g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}\odot g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> removes certain entries of <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and never increases its magnitude. Hence <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|M_{i}\odot g_{i}\|_{2}\leq\|g_{i}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|M_{i}\odot g_{i}\|_{2}\leq\|g_{i}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Multiplying by <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> yields the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Inter-Shard Stability)<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume masks <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{M_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are sampled independently with overlap probability <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then in expectation,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\langle M_{i}\odot g_{i},M_{j}\odot g_{j}\rangle]=\rho^{2}\langle g_{i},g_{j}\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\langle M_{i}\odot g_{i},M_{j}\odot g_{j}\rangle]=\rho^{2}\langle g_{i},g_{j}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus, masking reduces the expected conflict between gradients of different shards.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each coordinate <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr[M_{i}(p)=1,M_{j}(p)=1]=\rho^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[M_{i}(p)=1,M_{j}(p)=1]=\rho^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the expected inner product between masked gradients is <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> times the original inner product. This reduces cross-shard interference and improves stability.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#43C67A;">D.3  Closed-Loop Re-trigger Analysis</h3>

<div id="Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2</span></span><span id="Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Error Reduction per Re-trigger)<span id="Thmassumption2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that each re-trigger reduces the error rate of shard <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> by at least a fixed constant <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, unless it is already below the pruning threshold <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>prune</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Linear Error Decrease)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the error rate after <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> re-triggers. Under Assumption 2,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(n)}\leq r_{i}^{(0)}-n\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(n)}\leq r_{i}^{(0)}-n\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Finite-Time Convergence)<span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the initial error rate, then after at most</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq\frac{r_{i}^{(0)}-\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}}{\delta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>prune</mi></msub></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq\frac{r_{i}^{(0)}-\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}}{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">re-triggers, the error rate satisfies <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(N)}\leq\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>prune</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(N)}\leq\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma 3, <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(N)}\leq r_{i}^{(0)}-N\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(N)}\leq r_{i}^{(0)}-N\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Choosing <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(0)}-N\delta\leq\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>prune</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(0)}-N\delta\leq\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures convergence below threshold in finite time.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#43C67A;">D.4  Overall Convergence Intuition</h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Closed-Loop Stability of REPAIR)<span id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions 1 and 2, the iterative process combining masked updates, inner-batch distillation, and closed-loop re-trigger forms a contractive mapping in expectation. Consequently, the system converges to a stable edited state with a bounded error rate and without catastrophic forgetting.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof Sketch.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Masked updates reduce the variance of parameter updates, inner-batch distillation aligns outputs across samples, and re-trigger guarantees finite-time reduction of shard-level error rates. Together, these components yield monotone improvement. By standard stochastic contraction arguments, the process converges to a fixed point characterized by consistent batch predictions and an error rate below <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>prune</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Zero-variance at any global minimizer)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}o_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}o_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{var}}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i}\|o_{i}-\mu\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{var}}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i}\|o_{i}-\mu\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If not all <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are equal, then <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{var}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{var}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, while if <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{1}=\cdots=o_{m}=v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{1}=\cdots=o_{m}=v</annotation></semantics></math> (with <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v\|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v\|=1</annotation></semantics></math>) then <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{var}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{var}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence every global minimizer of <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KD</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{S}^{d-1})^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{S}^{d-1})^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> must satisfy <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{1}=\cdots=o_{m}=:v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{1}=\cdots=o_{m}=:v</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Unique global minimizer)<span id="Thmlemma4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the conclusion of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Zero-variance at any global minimizer). ‣ D.4 Overall Convergence Intuition ‣ Appendix D Theoretical Analysis and Proof Sketches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, minimizing
<math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}(v)=\lambda\bigl(1-\langle v,u\rangle\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KD</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}(v)=\lambda\bigl(1-\langle v,u\rangle\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v\|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v\|=1</annotation></semantics></math>
gives the unique solution <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\star}=u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\star}=u</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore the unique global minimizer of <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KD</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{S}^{d-1})^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{S}^{d-1})^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\star}=[u,\ldots,u]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\star}=[u,\ldots,u]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Riemannian smoothness)<span id="Thmlemma5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=(\mathbb{S}^{d-1})^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=(\mathbb{S}^{d-1})^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and endow each block with the canonical metric.
Then <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KD</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth on <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> in the Riemannian sense:
there exists a constant</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}_{R}\;\leq\;\frac{2\lambda}{m}+\frac{4\vartheta}{m}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϑ</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}_{R}\;\leq\;\frac{2\lambda}{m}+\frac{4\vartheta}{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">such that for all <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S,S^{\prime}\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S,S^{\prime}\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\operatorname{grad}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}(S)-\operatorname{grad}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}(S^{\prime})\|\leq\mathsf{L}_{R}\,\operatorname{dist}_{\mathcal{M}}(S,S^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>grad</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KD</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>grad</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KD</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>dist</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\operatorname{grad}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}(S)-\operatorname{grad}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}(S^{\prime})\|\leq\mathsf{L}_{R}\,\operatorname{dist}_{\mathcal{M}}(S,S^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.
<em id="Thmlemma5.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">Sketch.</em> For each block <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{o_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cos}}=-(\lambda/m)u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>cos</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{o_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cos}}=-(\lambda/m)u</annotation></semantics></math> (constant),
and <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{o_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{var}}=(2\vartheta/m)(o_{i}-\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>var</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϑ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{o_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{var}}=(2\vartheta/m)(o_{i}-\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> depending linearly on <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{o_{j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{o_{j}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Projecting to the tangent space by <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I-o_{i}o_{i}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I-o_{i}o_{i}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math> and using the Lipschitzness of the projection map on <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> yields the bound.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Convergence of cosine+variance KD on the sphere)<span id="Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider Riemannian gradient descent on <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=(\mathbb{S}^{d-1})^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=(\mathbb{S}^{d-1})^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i}^{(t+1)}\;=\;R_{\,o_{i}^{(t)}}\!\bigl(-\eta_{t}\,\operatorname{grad}_{o_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}(S_{t})\bigr)\quad(i=1,\ldots,m)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>grad</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KD</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i}^{(t+1)}\;=\;R_{\,o_{i}^{(t)}}\!\bigl(-\eta_{t}\,\operatorname{grad}_{o_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}(S_{t})\bigr)\quad(i=1,\ldots,m),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with the retraction <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{o}(v)=(o+v)/\|o+v\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{o}(v)=(o+v)/\|o+v\|</annotation></semantics></math>. If the step sizes satisfy either
(a) a constant stepsize <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta_{t}&lt;2/\mathsf{L}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta_{t}&lt;2/\mathsf{L}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, or
(b) diminishing stepsizes <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\eta_{t}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\eta_{t}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\eta_{t}^{2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\eta_{t}^{2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>,
then:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}(S_{t})\downarrow\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}(S^{\star}),\qquad\|\operatorname{grad}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}(S_{t})\|\to 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KD</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KD</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>grad</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KD</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}(S_{t})\downarrow\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}(S^{\star}),\qquad\|\operatorname{grad}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KD}}(S_{t})\|\to 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and every limit point of <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a Riemannian critical point. By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4 (Unique global minimizer). ‣ D.4 Overall Convergence Intuition ‣ Appendix D Theoretical Analysis and Proof Sketches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>,
the unique global minimizer is <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\star}=[u,\ldots,u]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\star}=[u,\ldots,u]</annotation></semantics></math>; thus the sequence converges to <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof sketch.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Riemannian smoothness (Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5 (Riemannian smoothness). ‣ D.4 Overall Convergence Intuition ‣ Appendix D Theoretical Analysis and Proof Sketches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) on the compact manifold <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>
ensures the standard descent lemma and monotone decrease for RGD under <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta&lt;2/\mathsf{L}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta&lt;2/\mathsf{L}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,
implying convergence of function values and gradients to zero. By Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Zero-variance at any global minimizer). ‣ D.4 Overall Convergence Intuition ‣ Appendix D Theoretical Analysis and Proof Sketches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>–<a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4 (Unique global minimizer). ‣ D.4 Overall Convergence Intuition ‣ Appendix D Theoretical Analysis and Proof Sketches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, the only global minimizer is <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence all limit points coincide with <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#43C67A;">D.5  Stability of Masked Gradient Updates</h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}=\nabla_{W_{v,i}^{\prime}}\mathcal{L}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}=\nabla_{W_{v,i}^{\prime}}\mathcal{L}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. A coordinate mask <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}\in\{0,1\}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}\in\{0,1\}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> acts by <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M_{i}\odot g_{i})_{p}=M_{i}(p)\,g_{i,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M_{i}\odot g_{i})_{p}=M_{i}(p)\,g_{i,p}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6</span></span><span id="Thmlemma6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Norm Bound under Masked Updates)<span id="Thmlemma6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any stepsize <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the masked update <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{v,i}^{\prime}=-\eta(M_{i}\odot g_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{v,i}^{\prime}=-\eta(M_{i}\odot g_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta W_{v,i}^{\prime}\|_{2}\leq\eta\,\|g_{i}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta W_{v,i}^{\prime}\|_{2}\leq\eta\,\|g_{i}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Coordinate-wise, <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|M_{i}(p)\,g_{i,p}|\leq|g_{i,p}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|M_{i}(p)\,g_{i,p}|\leq|g_{i,p}|</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}(p)\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}(p)\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|M_{i}\odot g_{i}\|_{2}\leq\|g_{i}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|M_{i}\odot g_{i}\|_{2}\leq\|g_{i}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and multiplying by <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> yields the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Inter-Shard Inner-Product Scaling)<span id="Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that for each coordinate <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, the masks <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}(p),M_{j}(p)\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}(p),M_{j}(p)\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> are sampled independently with</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[M_{i}(p)=1]=\Pr[M_{j}(p)=1]=\rho,\quad 0\leq\rho\leq 1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[M_{i}(p)=1]=\Pr[M_{j}(p)=1]=\rho,\quad 0\leq\rho\leq 1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and masks are independent across coordinates and independent of <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i},g_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i},g_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, conditional on <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i},g_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i},g_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\langle M_{i}\odot g_{i},\,M_{j}\odot g_{j}\rangle\,\middle|\,g_{i},g_{j}\right]=\rho^{2}\,\langle g_{i},g_{j}\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\langle M_{i}\odot g_{i},\,M_{j}\odot g_{j}\rangle\,\middle|\,g_{i},g_{j}\right]=\rho^{2}\,\langle g_{i},g_{j}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, masking scales the expected cross-shard alignment/conflict by the factor <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By linearity of expectation and independence, for each coordinate <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A4.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[M_{i}(p)M_{j}(p)]=\mathbb{E}[M_{i}(p)]\,\mathbb{E}[M_{j}(p)]=\rho^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[M_{i}(p)M_{j}(p)]=\mathbb{E}[M_{i}(p)]\,\mathbb{E}[M_{j}(p)]=\rho^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Summing over <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> yields the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#43C67A;">D.6  Closed-Loop Re-trigger Analysis</h3>

<div id="Thmassumption3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3</span></span><span id="Thmassumption3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Error Reduction per Re-trigger)<span id="Thmassumption3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the error rate of shard <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> after <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> re-triggers. There exists <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that each re-trigger reduces error by at least <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(n)}&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>prune</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(n)}&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7</span></span><span id="Thmlemma7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Piecewise-Linear Error Decrease)<span id="Thmlemma7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Error Reduction per Re-trigger). ‣ D.6 Closed-Loop Re-trigger Analysis ‣ Appendix D Theoretical Analysis and Proof Sketches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, for all <math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(n)}\;\leq\;\max\!\bigl\{\,\tau_{\mathrm{prune}},\;r_{i}^{(0)}-n\delta\,\bigr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>prune</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(n)}\;\leq\;\max\!\bigl\{\,\tau_{\mathrm{prune}},\;r_{i}^{(0)}-n\delta\,\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(k)}&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>prune</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(k)}&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(k+1)}\leq r_{i}^{(k)}-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(k+1)}\leq r_{i}^{(k)}-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Once <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(k)}\leq\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>prune</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(k)}\leq\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the bound <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(n)}\leq\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>prune</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(n)}\leq\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}</annotation></semantics></math> propagates for all <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq k</annotation></semantics></math>. Unrolling gives the stated maximum form.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Finite-Time Hitting the Pruning Threshold)<span id="Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\star}\;=\;\Bigl\lceil\frac{(r_{i}^{(0)}-\tau_{\mathrm{prune}})_{+}}{\delta}\Bigr\rceil\quad\text{where }(x)_{+}:=\max\{x,0\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>prune</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\star}\;=\;\Bigl\lceil\frac{(r_{i}^{(0)}-\tau_{\mathrm{prune}})_{+}}{\delta}\Bigr\rceil\quad\text{where }(x)_{+}:=\max\{x,0\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">After at most <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> re-triggers, we have <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(N_{\star})}\leq\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>prune</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(N_{\star})}\leq\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma7" title="Lemma 7 (Piecewise-Linear Error Decrease). ‣ D.6 Closed-Loop Re-trigger Analysis ‣ Appendix D Theoretical Analysis and Proof Sketches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, choose the smallest integer <math id="A4.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(0)}-N_{\star}\delta\leq\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>prune</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(0)}-N_{\star}\delta\leq\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A4.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{(N_{\star})}\leq\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>prune</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{(N_{\star})}\leq\tau_{\mathrm{prune}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Algorithms</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The pseudocode for error feedback, network pruning, sample knowledge distillation and reintegration, and the loss-based weighted ties merge strategy is as follows:</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> REPAIR: Closed-Loop Lifelong Model Editing (Training)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Pretrained model </span><math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; target FFN value matrix </span><math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">W</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{v}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; #shards </span><math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">;
mask ratio </span><math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; thresholds </span><math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon,\tau_{E},\tau_{\text{prune}},\tau_{\text{correct}},\epsilon_{\text{cons}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">prune</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">correct</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">cons</mtext></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon,\tau_{E},\tau_{\text{prune}},\tau_{\text{correct}},\epsilon_{\text{cons}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">;
margins </span><math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; KD weights </span><math id="alg1.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda,\vartheta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϑ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda,\vartheta)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> for Eq.(4);
routing-loss weight </span><math id="alg1.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{a}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; batch size </span><math id="alg1.l1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; optional temperature </span><math id="alg1.l1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> for soft KD.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
